.TH INZONE-GUI 1 "2026-10-04" "inzone-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inzone-gui \- control INZONE headset profiles and settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inzone-gui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inzone-gui
opens the Qt Quick desktop interface for audio profiles, equalizer settings,
microphone levels, headset controls, and application profile rules.
It communicates with
.B inzone-service
on the desktop user's session D-Bus.
.PP
The desktop application identifier and D-Bus service name are
.BR dev.zeroday0619 .
The interface selects native Wayland in a Wayland session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Verify that an application window becomes visible and exit after two seconds.
.TP
.BI "--screenshot " PATH
Save an image of the application window to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI "--diagnostics " PATH
Write JSON diagnostics for the Qt platform, application identity, display
scaling, and rendering backend. Use
.B -
to write JSON to standard output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Override automatic Qt platform selection, for example with
.B wayland
or
.BR offscreen .
.SH SETUP
Initialize audio configuration and acquire the separate Sony DSP assets with
.BR inzone-tools (1)
before applying an audio profile for the first time.
Package installation does not initialize a user's audio configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inzone-profile (1),
.BR inzone-service (1),
.BR inzone-tools (1)
